# Licence of the captured data

**Crawl permission: established. Reuse: not established.**

## Crawling

Checked 2026-09-25. `apps.shopify.com/robots.txt` permits `/browse/` and the
sitemaps, and disallows every query string:

    Disallow: /internal/
    Disallow: /services/
    Disallow: /*?*shpxid=*
    Disallow: /*?*auth=*

plus a blanket `Disallow: /*?*` form covering query URLs, which closes
`/search?q=`. The captured endpoint, `sitemap_apps_en.xml`, carries no query
string and is permitted.

Evaluated with longest-match (`wss.robots`) as RFC 9309 and Google specify, not
`urllib.robotparser`, which returns the first matching rule and is wrong on rule
sets of this shape.

## Reuse

**Unaddressed.** No licence statement appears in the sitemap or on the store
pages, and Shopify's terms have not been read for a redistribution grant. Do not
assert one.

What this repository holds is **a list of URLs the publisher publishes for search
engines**, plus counts derived from it. There is no app content — no description,
no pricing, no developer, no screenshots — because the sitemap contains none and
the detail pages are deliberately not fetched.

## Personal data

None. The sitemap carries app slugs only. Developer names appear on detail pages,
which this repo does not capture.
